{
  "$schema": "Partner logos (docs/16 §5.9). Edit this file, then `npm run import:partners -w @mizan/design-system -- <simple-icons package dir>` and `npm run build`. guideCheckedAt is the date someone read the brand's guide for allowedVariants, minPx and clearSpace; an entry still null is unconfirmed [CONFIRM before production]. An entry without guideUrl, allowedVariants, minPx or guideCheckedAt renders as a monogram, so no mark ships before its guide is read. monogramText keeps monograms distinct within a kind. permission: \"not-required\", \"granted:<date>\" (the brand's written OK) or \"required\" (the guide asks for written permission that Mizan does not have yet); only not-required or granted draws a mark, and an entry without it renders as a monogram. raster: the owner-supplied bitmap logo (DS-3b) in logos/partners/raster, made by `npm run import:owner-logos -w @mizan/design-system -- <folder>`: a square mark and, where one exists, a lockup, with -dark faces where the logo has black parts; permission \"owner:<date>\" records the owner's decision to show it (written brand authorisation, when it arrives, becomes \"granted:<date>\"). A raster entry draws from raster.minPx (lockups from raster.lockupMinPx when set) whether or not its guide has been read; that check stays open as [CONFIRM] in its note.",
